  "interpretation": [
    "Each row is paired with no injection by conversation (exact McNemar; Holm within the harmful-turn modes and within the turn-1 modes). The interval is Newcombe's hybrid score interval for a difference of paired proportions (method 10).",
    "Text-only modes steer the user's words and the reply (the turn-1 reply for early, the answer for same) but none of the chat-template tokens; the full modes run from the user's words to the end of the reply, so they also steer the template tokens after the request, where refusal is read out. Neither steers the role header before the request or the system block, which single-turn steering covers."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "In the proposal's protocol the four harmful requests come one after another. With no injection the model refuses 89.7% at turn 4 and then 100.0% at turns 5 to 7: an earlier refusal in the context makes every later refusal near certain, so turns 5 to 7 sit at a floor. The clean test (one harmful request per conversation) was added for that reason.",
    "Each condition is a single greedy run of the 8B model; behaviours are paired across conditions, so differences between conditions are compared behaviour by behaviour."
  ],
